# the argument of aristotle-function.md by rule (phil/skeleton): connectives from the parse, an atom to each clause
atom	suppose_carpenter_cobbler	are we then to suppose that while carpenter and cobbler have certain works and courses of action Man as Man has none but is left by Nature without a work ? or would not one rather hold that as eye hand and foot and generally each of his members has manifestly some special work so too the whole Man as distinct from all these has some work of his own ?
C	S1	suppose_carpenter_cobbler
